<p>Loads a cutscene.
</p>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Void%20keyword" title="Void keyword">void</a> CS_LoadCutscene(<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Resource%20keyword" title="Resource keyword">resource</a> rCutscene,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> strPlot&#160;= "",<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nPlotFlag&#160;= -1,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sTalkSpeaker&#160;= ""<br />);</div>
<dl>
<dt>Parameters:
<dd><dl><dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">rCutscene<dd>Cutscene resource (CUTSCENE_* constants defined in cutscenes_h.nss)<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">strPlot<dd>Plot which contains the flag to be set<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">nPlotFlag<dd>Plot flag to be set<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">sTalkSpeaker<dd>Tag of creature who will initiate dialogue
</dl>
</dl><dl><dt>Returns:
<p><dd>Nothing.
</p>
</dl><dl><dt>Source:
<p><dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Core%20Resources" title="Core Resources (page does not exist)">Core Resources</a>.<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Utility%20h" title="Utility h">utility_h</a>
</p>
</dl>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Loads the specified cutscene. Sets the specified plot flag after the cutscene plays (optional), and makes sTalkSpeaker initiate dialog with the player (also optional).
</p><p>Note: The plot flag and talk speaker parameters require the script gen00cs_cutscene_end.nss to be attached to the cutscene itself.
</p>
